Title: LIVE PROOF
Credit: Live feature verification fixture
Draft date: 5 September 2026

Note: every named person in this scene is invented for testing. "Senator
Corrigan" names no real senator, past or present, deliberately -- a fixture
that put a fabricated damaging claim in a real living person's mouth would be
the exact harm this product exists to catch, not a safe way to test it. The
song and the painting are real and are used for what they actually are: two
things with a genuine, checkable market and copyright status.

TITLE CARD: THIS IS A TRUE STORY.

FADE IN:

INT. COFFEE SHOP - DAY

MAYA GUTIERREZ, a journalist in her thirties, sits with a laptop. A paper cup
on the table is branded KESTREL COFFEE. A framed print of Edward Hopper's
"Nighthawks" hangs on the wall behind her, clearly visible for several
seconds.

Her phone plays a track through a tinny speaker.

MAYA
(to herself)
That's "Landslide" by Fleetwood Mac.

DANIEL REYES enters, sits across from her. He has a small tattoo of a
compass on his forearm, visible as he sets down his bag.

DANIEL
You look like you haven't slept.

MAYA
I've been going through the Corrigan file all night.

DANIEL
The senator?

MAYA
Senator Corrigan has never once testified before Congress on this. Not
once. He's lied about it in every interview for six years.

DANIEL
That's a hell of a thing to put in print.

MAYA
It's true. I have the transcripts.

DANIEL
Even if it's true, running it under a "true story" card means every word
about him gets read as fact by every viewer who sees this.

MAYA
Then we'd better be right.

FADE OUT.
